NumPy & Pandas for Data Analysis

Overview

This repository focuses on NumPy and Pandas, two essential Python libraries for data analysis and preprocessing. It includes practical examples, exercises, and notebooks covering data manipulation, transformation, and analysis.

Topics Covered

NumPy

- NumPy Arrays
- Array Indexing & Slicing
- Reshaping Arrays
- Mathematical Operations
- Broadcasting
- Aggregation Functions
- Random Module
- Linear Algebra Basics

Pandas

- Series & DataFrames
- Reading CSV & Excel Files
- Data Inspection
- Filtering & Sorting
- Handling Missing Values
- Removing Duplicates
- GroupBy Operations
- Merge & Join
- Pivot Tables
- Data Transformation
- Date & Time Operations
- Exporting Processed Data

Folder Structure

NumPy-and-Pandas/
│── NumPy/
│── Pandas/
│── Practice/
│── Datasets/
│── Notebooks/
└── README.md

Learning Outcomes

- Perform efficient numerical computations using NumPy.
- Analyze and manipulate datasets with Pandas.
- Prepare datasets for Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and Machine Learning.
- Build a strong foundation for Data Analytics and Data Science.

Tools Used

- Python 3.x
- NumPy
- Pandas
- Jupyter Notebook
- VS Code

Status

Actively learning and implementing real-world data analysis workflows using NumPy and Pandas.
